## Updating from Template

The template may receive improvements over time. To update this project:

```bash
copier update --trust
```

**Before updating**:
1. Commit all local changes
2. Review [python-kit's CHANGELOG](https://github.com/danielnaab/python-kit/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)
   for the versions between this project's `_commit` (in `.copier-answers.yml`) and the new one
3. Test after updating

Copier will:
- Preserve files in `_skip_if_exists` (your customizations)
- Update template-managed files
- Show conflicts for manual resolution
- Run the template's migrations for the versions it crosses (`_migrations` in python-kit's `copier.yml`)
{% if graft_docs %}
`scions/python-kit` is a git submodule at the python-kit tag this project was generated or last updated from.
After the update, move it to the tag you updated to: `nix run .#graft upgrade python-kit@vX.Y.Z`. Commit the
moved `scions/python-kit` with the update. `flake.nix` is this project's: the update doesn't touch it. The
weekly PR below does all of this.

### The weekly update PR

`.forgejo/workflows/python-kit-upgrade.yaml` runs weekly (Mondays 06:41 UTC): if python-kit has a newer
tag in the major this project is on, it runs `copier update` to it, moves `scions/python-kit` to that tag
(`graft upgrade python-kit@vX.Y.Z`), commits, then runs `nix flake check`, `graft check` and the tests on the
commit, pushes the result to `python-kit/upgrade` and opens a PR quoting python-kit's CHANGELOG. Conflicts
and failing checks are pushed too, and named in the PR's title. A new major is never taken: the run warns,
and you update by hand after reading its Upgrading section. It opens the PR with the same
`GRAFT_PR_TOKEN` secret as graft's bot (below), and leaves a PR that changes `.forgejo/` workflows for
you to open after reading the diff. The file is template-managed: delete it to stop the bot.
{% endif %}
