{% if graft_docs %}
### Keeping the grafted docs current

Each folder in `scions/` is a git submodule (`scions/README.md` says more): another repository, checked out at
a release tag. After a clone, fill them with `git submodule update --init` (or `nix run .#graft sync`); Nix
fetches them itself for `nix flake check`.

- `.forgejo/workflows/graft-check.yaml` checks on every PR that every scion is a registered submodule at a
  release tag, that graft's workflows are current, and that the flake evaluates.
- `.forgejo/workflows/graft-upgrade.yaml` runs weekly: if graft or knowledge-base-kit has a newer
  tag in its major, it opens a PR moving to it, gated by the whole `nix flake check` and quoting
  the provider's CHANGELOG. Both workflows carry `# managed by graft` and move with graft's pin;
  delete that line to keep your own edits. python-kit's own pin moves with the
  python-kit-upgrade PR above, not this bot.
  On a private repo Forgejo won't let the job token open a PR, so the bot uses the Actions secret
  `GRAFT_PR_TOKEN`: a `write:repository` token for a bot user (steward), so you review its PRs.
  A user-level secret (your Settings > Actions > Secrets) covers every repo you own; a repo-level
  one covers just this repo. Without it the run pushes `graft/upgrade` and fails with a compare link.
- By hand: `nix run .#graft outdated`, `nix run .#graft upgrade`, `nix run .#graft check`.
